    {
      "key": "team.reading.a2.cooking-grandma",
      "kind": "ReadingPassage",
      "values": {
        "Title": "Cooking with Grandma",
        "Content": "On Sunday I cook with my grandma in our small kitchen. She teaches me how to wash vegetables and cut them carefully on a board. We also boil rice and prepare a light soup with carrots and onions. I try to remember each step so I can help again next time without asking too many questions.\n\nWhen the food is ready, the kitchen smells wonderful. We set the table and share the meal with my parents. Everyone says the soup tastes better because we made it together. My father asks for a second bowl and smiles.\n\nCooking together makes me feel close to my family. Next week grandma says we will bake a simple cake for dessert. I already bought flour and sugar so we can start early in the morning.",
        "Level": "A2",
        "Topic": "Food",
        "ImageUrl": "asset:26df69c2262a89ca32ba933fb0c5216fa0fb6a6ce6b87da6964cdbbc1e1136f3.jpg",
